            "description": "ISO-8601 date-time with offset, e.g. 1914-08-04T08:00:00Z"
          },
          "end": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "date-time",
            "pattern": "^(?:(?:\\d\\d[2468][048]|\\d\\d[13579][26]|\\d\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\d|2[0-8])))T(?:(?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d(?::[0-5]\\d(?:\\.\\d+)?)?(?:Z|([+-](?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d)))$",
            "description": "ISO-8601 date-time with offset, e.g. 1914-08-04T08:00:00Z"
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "start",
          "end"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "description": "Inclusive time range; start must precede end"
      },
      "window": {
        "description": "What timeRange means, when it is not the obvious thing. Absent: it is when this happened, inside the pack window. \"placed\": it is where a chapter sits on the campaign strip, not when it happened — the beats carry the real dates in dateLabel. \"outside\": it is when this happened, and that is outside the campaign — a prologue or an epilogue, which keeps its own clock.",
